This patch addresses a repository-controlled shell injection vulnerability in the VERIFY build checks where unsanitized file paths, test names, and identifiers were being concatenated directly into shell commands executed via `sh -c`. The vulnerability was mitigated by implementing the `shellQuote()` function to properly escape all user-controlled inputs before shell command execution. The fixes were applied to `internal/sem/search_verify.go` to escape directory paths and other command parameters, with corresponding test coverage added in `internal/sem/search_verify_test.go` to verify the escaping behavior prevents shell metacharacter injection attacks.","title":"[Aikido] Fix shell injection vulnerability in VERIFY build checks by escaping file paths","base":"main","base_sha":"8f6764d69648f76ce0fe37f9f0e2e8433fdbea5a","head":"fix/aikido-security-code-audit-86369498-exvw","head_sha":"ee6303ff51aa03049440d8944a85f0a7981c2063","merge_commit_sha":"18bb6573718f21da2afeb4711579def59a8b804b","user":{"login":"aikido-autofix[bot]","name":"aikido-autofix[bot]","email":null,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/268977?v=4","id":119856028},"requested_reviewers":null,"requested_team_reviewers":null,"diff":null,"comments":null,"created_at":"2026-08-11T17:04:32Z","updated_at":"2026-08-11T17:04:44Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"commits":1,"changed_files":2,"additions":111,"deletions":17,"display_url":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/90","display_title":"[Aikido] Fix shell injection vulnerability in VERIFY build checks by escaping file paths"}
