 55		// authority as the root .gitignore, and Git applies both. Reading only
 56		// .gitignore silently pulled excluded trees into the working-tree scan.
 57		//
 58		// It is NOT always at <repo>/.git/info/exclude. In a linked worktree, <repo>/.git
 59		// is a regular file holding "gitdir: <path>", so that join names a path under a
 60		// non-directory: os.Stat returns ENOTDIR rather than ErrNotExist, and treating
 61		// that as fatal aborted the entire search with zero results in every worktree.
